[h2]The dirt is real. That is the whole point.[/h2]
Most cleaning games erase a mask. Refluff does not. Under the pile runs a fluid simulation: water soaks in and wicks sideways, foam piles into mounds and slowly collapses, dust turns to mud the moment it gets wet, and dried crust has to be broken before anything will shift it. Push slurry with the squeegee and it heaps up in front of the blade. Leave a patch damp and it stays damp until you dry it.

The pile is a real 3D surface, not a flat texture. It presses down under water and stands back up as it dries.

[h2]Ten tools, and an order to use them in[/h2]
Crust first: the scraper chips it loose, the dry vacuum takes the crumbs. Then water - the hose to soak, foam to lift grime out of the fibers, the rotary brush to work it down to the backing. Then take it all back out: squeegee, wet vacuum, dryer.

Order matters. Soak a carpet full of dry dust and you get mud. Foam over dried crust and nothing happens until you have chipped it off. And everything you knock loose lands on the floor, which is why there is a detergent sprayer and a mop as well.

[h2]A different carpet every time[/h2]
Every job rolls a new rug: a different pattern, a different amount of dirt, a different mix of dust, grime, crust and spills. Some arrive almost clean. Some take a while. Underneath all of it are photographs of five real museum carpets.

[h2]Then you get paid[/h2]
Hand the carpet over and the slip prints line by line: base rate, speed bonus, 100% clean, bone dry, and a combo if you land both. Spend it on POWER and AREA upgrades for any tool, or on inspection lamps that show you the moisture and the dirt your eyes cannot find yet.

[h2]Headphones on[/h2]
Every machine is a recording of a real one. Motors spool up and wind down as you work, the vacuum tube rattles at the exact moment it swallows a crumb, water hisses, foam fizzes, bristles drag.

[h2]No pressure[/h2]
No enemies. No fail state. No timer running out - the speed bonus only ever adds.

[list]
[*]Single player
[*]Mouse and keyboard; no controller support
[*]English interface
[*]Requires a DirectX 12 graphics card
[/list]
